WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.660
Third Night Today has been a dreary, rain

2
00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:08.340
-soaked day, one without even the faintest trace

3
00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:08.940
of sunlight.

4
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.620
It's as though the sky itself is reflecting

5
00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:13.820
the gloom in my heart, the weight of

6
00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.900
thoughts pressing down on me like the clouds

7
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:16.320
above.

8
00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:19.700
The rain feels endless like the old age

9
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.880
that stretches out before me, colorless and joyless.

10
00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:27.440
My mind is restless, swarming with strange, unanswerable

11
00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:30.720
questions, each one darker and more oppressive than

12
00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:31.299
the last.

13
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:37.300
These questions—so heavy, so impossible—seem to crowd my

14
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.000
brain all at once, leaving me feeling powerless.

15
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:42.320
I can't bring myself to resolve them.

16
00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:44.740
Perhaps it's not for me to settle such

17
00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:45.080
things.

18
00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:47.820
Perhaps they are meant to remain unanswered.

19
00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:49.660
Today we won't meet.

20
00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:52.940
Yesterday, when we said good-bye, the sky

21
00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:54.040
was already changing.

22
00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.660
Clouds began to gather on the horizon, and

23
00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:01.020
a thin mist rose, veiling the city in

24
00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:01.840
a gray haze.

25
00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:05.180
I remember mentioning it as we parted, almost

26
00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:06.920
as if I could predict what was coming.

27
00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:10.420
Tomorrow will be a bad day, I had

28
00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:10.700
said.

29
00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.000
But she said nothing in return, refusing to

30
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.140
acknowledge even the possibility of rain.

31
00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:19.600
For her, the world was too bright, too

32
00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:21.660
full of happiness to imagine otherwise.

33
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.060
If it rains, we won't see each other,

34
00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:26.360
she had said simply.

35
00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:27.540
I won't come.

36
00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:30.960
I wanted to believe she wouldn't notice the

37
00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:33.920
rain today, that her happiness would overpower any

38
00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:34.380
storm.

39
00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:36.160
But she hasn't come.

40
00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:40.120
Yesterday was our third meeting, our third white

41
00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:43.720
night, a night so pure and fleeting, glowing

42
00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:45.840
with a light that seemed to promise eternity.

43
00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:49.340
And yet, here I am, alone.

44
00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:52.960
How radiant joy and happiness make a person,

45
00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:55.760
how it fills every corner of their being.

46
00:01:56.540 --> 00:02:00.140
Her heart was brimming yesterday, overflowing with love

47
00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:00.800
and excitement.

48
00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:03.600
You could see it in her every word,

49
00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.940
every gesture, every glance.

50
00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:08.440
It was as if she wanted the whole

51
00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:11.340
world to share in her joy, to bask

52
00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:12.200
in her happiness.

53
00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:15.540
There was a warmth in her voice, a

54
00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:17.820
tenderness in her words that made me feel

55
00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.520
as though they were meant just for me.

56
00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.860
How solicitous, how kind she was yesterday.

57
00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:26.360
How she tried so earnestly to encourage me,

58
00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:27.820
to lift my spirits.

59
00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:31.060
Oh, the irresistible coquetry of happiness.

60
00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:33.580
How easily it deceives.

61
00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.760
While she laughed and spoke with such tenderness,

62
00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:38.900
I—I believed it all.

63
00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:41.780
I thought it was real, that it came

64
00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:43.820
from her heart, and that it was meant

65
00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:44.200
for me.

66
00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:46.440
But my God, how could I have been

67
00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:47.200
so blind?

68
00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.060
How could I have fooled myself so completely?

69
00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:52.220
How could I not have seen that everything

70
00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:55.860
I thought was mine—her kindness, her smiles, her

71
00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:57.920
gentle words—belonged to another?

72
00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:00.220
None of it was truly mine.

73
00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:04.100
Even her tenderness towards me, her attentiveness, her

74
00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:07.800
affectionate concern—yes, even what I dared to think

75
00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.900
of as her love for me was nothing

76
00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:12.340
but an extension of her own joy, a

77
00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:14.580
joy that didn't originate from me, but from

78
00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:16.280
the thought of seeing someone else.

79
00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:18.980
I was nothing more than a bystander to

80
00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:21.300
her happiness, a piece of her world that

81
00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.540
she wished to include in her glowing anticipation

82
00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:25.060
of someone else.

83
00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:28.140
When he didn't come, when her hopes went

84
00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:30.160
unanswered, I saw her falter.

85
00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:33.600
The lightness in her step, the gaiety in

86
00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:36.260
her words—it all began to fade.

87
00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:40.100
Her laughter grew quieter, her movements more hesitant.

88
00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:43.880
And yet, strangely, she turned her attentiveness back

89
00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:46.240
to me, almost as if by instinct.

90
00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.160
It was as though, in the absence of

91
00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:51.580
her own happiness, she was trying to pass

92
00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:53.600
it on to me, to share what little

93
00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:54.800
she could still muster.

94
00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:58.180
I saw then how deeply she was affected.

95
00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:01.440
My nastenka—yes, I still dared to think of

96
00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:06.020
her as mine—was disheartened, dismayed, perhaps even heartbroken.

97
00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:09.220
I think in that moment she realized the

98
00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:11.160
truth—that I loved her.

99
00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:14.700
She saw my poor unspoken love reflected in

100
00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:17.519
my silence and in my eyes, and she

101
00:04:17.519 --> 00:04:18.579
felt sorry for me.

102
00:04:19.339 --> 00:04:21.540
When we are unhappy, it's as though we

103
00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:23.800
become more attuned to the suffering of others,

104
00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:26.660
as though our own pain sharpens our ability

105
00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:27.800
to recognize it.

106
00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:31.600
Instead of destroying our capacity to feel, sadness

107
00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:33.700
concentrates it, heightens it.

108
00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:37.020
She must have felt my sorrow, even as

109
00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:38.260
she wrestled with her own.

110
00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:40.460
I had gone to meet her with a

111
00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:43.340
full heart, carrying with me all the anticipation

112
00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:46.180
and impatience of someone who has allowed himself

113
00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:46.800
to hope.

114
00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:49.620
I had no idea then that it would

115
00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:52.240
end this way, that my hopes would crumble

116
00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:53.260
so completely.

117
00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.640
When I arrived, she was already there, waiting

118
00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:57.120
for me.

119
00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:00.480
She looked radiant, her face aglow with pleasure.

120
00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:04.080
She was expecting something—no, someone.

121
00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:07.680
She was expecting an answer, and that answer

122
00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:08.500
was him.

123
00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:11.840
She had arrived long before I did, her

124
00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:14.080
excitement so great that she couldn't wait.

125
00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:17.160
At first she was giddy, laughing at everything

126
00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:18.980
I said, even when it wasn't meant to

127
00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:19.420
be funny.

128
00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:22.500
Her laughter was infectious, but it didn't take

129
00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:24.340
long for me to sense the undercurrent of

130
00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:25.300
tension beneath it.

131
00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:27.880
I tried to talk to keep the conversation

132
00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:30.520
light, but soon I fell silent, unable to

133
00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:31.200
match her mood.

134
00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:33.600
I was too aware of the truth that

135
00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:35.120
she couldn't yet admit to herself.

136
00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:38.660
Do you know why I'm so happy today?

137
00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:41.720
she asked suddenly, her eyes sparkling as she

138
00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:42.260
turned to me.

139
00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:45.660
Do you know why I like looking at

140
00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:46.880
you so much right now?

141
00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:48.400
Why?

142
00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:50.780
I asked, trying to keep my voice steady,

143
00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:53.120
though my heart was already pounding in my

144
00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:53.480
chest.

145
00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:56.420
I like you, she said with a warm

146
00:05:56.420 --> 00:05:59.080
smile, because you haven't fallen in love with

147
00:05:59.080 --> 00:05:59.280
me.

148
00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:02.040
You know, in your place most men would

149
00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:05.000
have been sighing endlessly, pestering me with their

150
00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:08.380
feelings, making themselves miserable and me uncomfortable.

151
00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:11.280
But you, you're different.

152
00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:13.820
You're so nice about everything.

153
00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:18.140
She laughed softly, but before I could respond,

154
00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:20.400
she reached out and wrung my hand with

155
00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.120
such unexpected force that I almost cried out

156
00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:23.840
in surprise.

157
00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:26.940
Her laughter grew brighter at my startled expression,

158
00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:28.880
and for a moment her mood seemed to

159
00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:29.720
lift entirely.

160
00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:33.180
Goodness, what a friend you are, she said,

161
00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:36.260
her tone shifting into something more serious, even

162
00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:38.120
tender as her laughter subsided.

163
00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:41.400
She gazed at me intently, and after a

164
00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:45.200
pause she added, truly, God sent you to

165
00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:45.400
me.

166
00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:47.540
I don't know what I would have done

167
00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:49.020
without you, especially now.

168
00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:51.040
What would have happened to me if you

169
00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:51.860
hadn't been here?

170
00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:55.740
You are so unselfish, so kind, so understanding.

171
00:06:56.340 --> 00:06:59.360
How could anyone be more genuinely caring than

172
00:06:59.360 --> 00:06:59.640
you?

173
00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:02.360
When I am married, you and I will

174
00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:05.000
be the best of friends, closer than brother

175
00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:05.600
and sister.

176
00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:08.920
I shall care for you almost as much

177
00:07:08.920 --> 00:07:09.920
as I do for him.

178
00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:12.660
Her words pierced my heart.

179
00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:16.360
In that moment a wave of profound sadness

180
00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:18.880
swept over me, though I felt something else

181
00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:21.920
too, an inexplicable urge to laugh.

182
00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:25.120
Perhaps it was the absurdity of the situation,

183
00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:27.640
the strange mingling of my love for her,

184
00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:29.920
and the knowledge that she would never return

185
00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:30.160
it.

186
00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:33.500
You're very upset right now, I said gently,

187
00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:34.740
trying to steady my voice.

188
00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:36.580
You're frightened, aren't you?

189
00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:38.640
You're afraid he won't come.

190
00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:43.200
Oh, how unkind you are, she exclaimed, though

191
00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:45.260
there was no anger in her tone, only

192
00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:46.780
a kind of playful reproach.

193
00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:49.660
If I were less happy, I believe I

194
00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:51.900
would cry at your lack of faith, at

195
00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:53.880
your doubts about him, and at the way

196
00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:55.180
your scolding me now.

197
00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:57.080
But no, I won't cry.

198
00:07:57.320 --> 00:07:58.540
You've made me think, though.

199
00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:00.840
Yes, you've given me a great deal to

200
00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:03.220
think about, but not now, later.

201
00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:06.460
For now, I must admit, you're right.

202
00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:09.780
She sighed, her expression softening.

203
00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:12.540
Yes, I am not myself right now.

204
00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:15.000
I feel as though I'm floating, as though

205
00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.020
everything is unreal.

206
00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:18.960
My nerves are all on edge, and I

207
00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:20.820
can't seem to feel things as deeply as

208
00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:21.280
I should.

209
00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:24.500
Everything feels too light, too fragile.

210
00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:28.740
But enough about feelings, she said suddenly, cutting

211
00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:29.560
herself off.

212
00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:31.100
Let's not dwell on that.

213
00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:34.659
At that exact moment we heard footsteps approaching.

214
00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:37.419
The sound echoed faintly in the stillness of

215
00:08:37.419 --> 00:08:39.760
the night, growing louder as the figure drew

216
00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:40.200
closer.

217
00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:43.059
In the dim light we saw a form

218
00:08:43.059 --> 00:08:44.280
coming toward us.

219
00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:45.680
We both froze.

220
00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:50.040
She gasped softly, almost crying out, and I

221
00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:52.440
instinctively let go of her hand and took

222
00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:54.620
a step back, ready to walk away.

223
00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:57.420
But the figure passed by without stopping.

224
00:08:57.960 --> 00:08:58.860
It wasn't him.

225
00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:01.120
What are you afraid of?

226
00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:03.340
Why did you let go of my hand,

227
00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:05.640
she asked, turning to me with a puzzled

228
00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:06.140
expression.

229
00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:09.300
Without waiting for an answer, she reached out

230
00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:11.000
and placed her hand in mine again.

231
00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:13.340
Come, it's nothing.

232
00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:15.020
Let's wait together.

233
00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:17.920
When he comes, I want him to see

234
00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:19.560
how fond we are of each other.

235
00:09:20.420 --> 00:09:22.620
How fond we are of each other, I

236
00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:25.080
repeated, unable to hide the bitterness in my

237
00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:25.440
voice.

238
00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:29.200
Inside my heart ached as I thought, oh

239
00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:33.080
Nastenka, Nastenka, how much you've just revealed to

240
00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:34.060
me with those words.

241
00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:37.780
Such fondness in moments like this makes the

242
00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:40.880
heart grow cold and the soul unbearably heavy.

243
00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:44.680
Your hand is cold in mine, while mine

244
00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:45.860
burns like fire.

245
00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:49.300
How blind you are, Nastenka, to the truth

246
00:09:49.300 --> 00:09:50.280
right in front of you.

247
00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:54.160
Oh, how unbearable a happy person can be

248
00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:56.700
sometimes, and yet how could I ever be

249
00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:57.520
angry with you?

250
00:09:58.360 --> 00:10:01.940
The emotion swirling within me grew too intense

251
00:10:01.940 --> 00:10:02.620
to contain.

252
00:10:03.020 --> 00:10:05.680
At last my heart overflowed.

253
00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:08.300
Listen, Nastenka, I burst out.

254
00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:10.480
Do you have any idea how my day

255
00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:10.900
has been?

256
00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:13.140
Do you know what I've been feeling all

257
00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:13.720
this time?

258
00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:16.860
She looked at me with wide eyes, a

259
00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:18.700
mixture of curiosity and concern.

260
00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:20.300
What do you mean?

261
00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:22.120
How has your day been?

262
00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:23.280
Tell me.

263
00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:24.700
Tell me quickly.

264
00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:26.900
Why haven't you said anything until now?

265
00:10:26.900 --> 00:10:30.560
Well, I began struggling to find the right

266
00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:30.880
words.

267
00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:33.860
To start with, after I carried out all

268
00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:37.360
your commissions, delivering the letter, visiting your kind

269
00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:40.780
friends, then—then I went home and went straight

270
00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:41.220
to bed.

271
00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:43.520
Is that all?

272
00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:45.500
she interrupted, breaking into laughter.

273
00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:49.240
Yes, almost all, I answered, trying to hold

274
00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:52.500
myself together as foolish, inexplicable tears threatened to

275
00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:53.620
well up in my eyes.

276
00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:56.400
I woke up an hour before our appointment,

277
00:10:56.600 --> 00:10:57.880
though, truth be told.

278
00:10:58.380 --> 00:10:59.920
It felt as though I hadn't slept at

279
00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:00.220
all.

