356
00:14:06.100 --> 00:14:08.040
I regretted saying it immediately.

357
00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:11.540
The look of nervous uncertainty in her eyes,

358
00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:13.860
the way her voice trembled as she whispered,

359
00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:16.740
yes, it's eleven, filled me with a sharp

360
00:14:16.740 --> 00:14:17.540
pang of guilt.

361
00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:19.500
Why had I done that?

362
00:14:19.900 --> 00:14:22.420
Why had I deliberately reminded her of the

363
00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:22.800
time?

364
00:14:23.480 --> 00:14:26.380
I cursed myself for my petty impulse, for

365
00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:28.720
the spiteful satisfaction I had felt just a

366
00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:29.300
moment ago.

367
00:14:29.780 --> 00:14:32.860
She was anxious enough already, and now I

368
00:14:32.860 --> 00:14:33.720
had made it worse.

369
00:14:34.340 --> 00:14:36.600
I wanted to take it back, to undo

370
00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:38.980
the fear and sadness I had just caused.

371
00:14:39.780 --> 00:14:42.640
Now, Stenka, I said softly, trying to comfort

372
00:14:42.640 --> 00:14:46.340
her, don't worry, please, let's think this through

373
00:14:46.340 --> 00:14:47.060
rationally.

374
00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:49.800
There's no reason to believe the worst yet.

375
00:14:50.540 --> 00:14:53.280
There are so many possible explanations for why

376
00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:54.180
he hasn't come.

377
00:14:54.520 --> 00:14:56.500
Let me explain, and you'll see it's not

378
00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:57.520
as bad as it seems.

379
00:14:58.260 --> 00:15:00.800
She looked at me, her eyes wide and

380
00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:02.740
searching, desperate for reassurance.

381
00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:05.260
I knew she wanted to believe me, to

382
00:15:05.260 --> 00:15:07.320
hold on to hope, and it gave me

383
00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:08.700
the strength to press on.

384
00:15:09.940 --> 00:15:13.280
Look, I began, my voice growing steadier as

385
00:15:13.280 --> 00:15:14.400
I warmed to my task.

386
00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:17.920
It's entirely possible that he hasn't received your

387
00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:18.460
letter yet.

388
00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:20.900
Think about it, what if he wasn't at

389
00:15:20.900 --> 00:15:21.960
home when it arrived?

390
00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:24.600
He might not have read it, even now,

391
00:15:25.060 --> 00:15:26.880
or perhaps he read it but wasn't able

392
00:15:26.880 --> 00:15:28.040
to respond immediately.

393
00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:30.840
There are so many reasons why he might

394
00:15:30.840 --> 00:15:31.860
not be here yet.

395
00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:34.140
Suppose he's planning to answer the letter but

396
00:15:34.140 --> 00:15:35.280
