527
00:20:35.820 --> 00:20:37.660
Doesn't that prove that we aren't equals?

528
00:20:38.440 --> 00:20:42.640
No, Nastenka, I replied gently, my voice barely

529
00:20:42.640 --> 00:20:43.440
above a whisper.

530
00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:46.760
It doesn't prove that you aren't equals.

531
00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:50.100
It proves that you love him more than

532
00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:51.420
anything in the world.

533
00:20:52.160 --> 00:20:53.640
More than yourself, even.

534
00:20:54.720 --> 00:20:57.220
She looked at me with wide, thoughtful eyes,

535
00:20:57.540 --> 00:20:59.340
as though my words had struck a chord

536
00:20:59.340 --> 00:21:00.300
deep within her.

537
00:21:01.120 --> 00:21:04.060
Yes, she said at last, her voice tinged

538
00:21:04.060 --> 00:21:05.320
with naive sincerity.

539
00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:09.320
Yes, maybe you're right, but do you know

540
00:21:09.320 --> 00:21:10.340
what strikes me now?

541
00:21:11.180 --> 00:21:13.900
She paused, her tone growing more reflective.

542
00:21:14.440 --> 00:21:16.840
I'm not talking about him anymore, not about

543
00:21:16.840 --> 00:21:19.740
anyone in particular, just speaking generally.

544
00:21:20.280 --> 00:21:22.280
This is something I've thought about before.

545
00:21:22.860 --> 00:21:24.620
Why can't we all just be like brothers

546
00:21:24.620 --> 00:21:25.380
to one another?

547
00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:27.680
Why is it that even the best people

548
00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:29.900
seem to hide parts of themselves from others,

549
00:21:30.240 --> 00:21:31.780
as if they're keeping something back?

550
00:21:32.220 --> 00:21:34.460
Why can't we simply say what's in our

551
00:21:34.460 --> 00:21:38.060
hearts, openly and honestly, especially when we know

552
00:21:38.060 --> 00:21:40.060
our words won't be empty or meaningless?

553
00:21:40.920 --> 00:21:44.100
Instead, we put up walls, we act distant,

554
00:21:44.540 --> 00:21:47.000
and we make ourselves seem harsher than we

555
00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:47.640
really are.

556
00:21:48.360 --> 00:21:50.380
It's as if everyone is afraid to show

557
00:21:50.380 --> 00:21:53.140
their feelings, afraid to express them too quickly,

558
00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:55.500
as though they might somehow cheapen them by

559
00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:56.160
doing so.

560
00:21:57.020 --> 00:22:00.060
Oh, Nastenka, I said, my heart aching at

561
00:22:00.060 --> 00:22:00.560
her words.

562
00:22:00.800 --> 00:22:04.500
What you're saying is true, painfully true, but

563
00:22:04.500 --> 00:22:06.600
there are so many reasons for it, so

564
00:22:06.600 --> 00:22:08.080
many complicated reasons.

565
00:22:09.200 --> 00:22:12.440
Even as I spoke, I felt myself suppressing

566
00:22:12.440 --> 00:22:15.180
my own feelings more than ever, struggling to

567
00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:18.140
keep my voice calm, to conceal the turmoil

568
00:22:18.140 --> 00:22:19.260
raging within me.

569
00:22:20.080 --> 00:22:23.460
No, no, she said suddenly, her voice charged

570
00:22:23.460 --> 00:22:24.340
with deep emotion.

571
00:22:24.720 --> 00:22:27.420
You, for instance, you're not like other people.

572
00:22:27.700 --> 00:22:29.460
I don't even know how to explain what

573
00:22:29.460 --> 00:22:29.960
I mean.

574
00:22:31.000 --> 00:22:34.280
She hesitated, her words faltering as though she

575
00:22:34.280 --> 00:22:36.220
was trying to grasp something intangible.

576
00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:38.640
It's hard for me to put it into

577
00:22:38.640 --> 00:22:41.000
words, but it seems to me that you,

578
00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:44.740
right now, at this very moment, it seems

579
00:22:44.740 --> 00:22:47.040
to me that you're sacrificing something for me.

580
00:22:48.020 --> 00:22:50.560
Her voice softened as she added this, and

581
00:22:50.560 --> 00:22:54.040
she glanced at me briefly, almost shyly, as

582
00:22:54.040 --> 00:22:55.260
if afraid of my reaction.

583
00:22:56.440 --> 00:22:58.940
Forgive me for saying so, she went on

584
00:22:58.940 --> 00:23:01.600
timidly, her voice trembling as she tried to

585
00:23:01.600 --> 00:23:02.420
keep her composure.

586
00:23:03.240 --> 00:23:06.080
I'm just a simple girl, I've seen so

587
00:23:06.080 --> 00:23:08.720
little of life, and sometimes I feel like

588
00:23:08.720 --> 00:23:10.440
I don't even know how to say what

589
00:23:10.440 --> 00:23:11.200
I want to say.

590
00:23:11.960 --> 00:23:14.620
She smiled faintly, but there was a quiver

591
00:23:14.620 --> 00:23:16.940
in her lips, as though she was holding

592
00:23:16.940 --> 00:23:20.460
back something deeper, something she couldn't quite articulate.

593
00:23:20.460 --> 00:23:23.140
I only wanted to tell you that I'm

594
00:23:23.140 --> 00:23:23.560
grateful.

595
00:23:24.220 --> 00:23:26.180
I feel it, deeply.

596
00:23:27.220 --> 00:23:29.200
Oh, may God bless you for it.

597
00:23:29.960 --> 00:23:32.360
May He grant you happiness, more than you

598
00:23:32.360 --> 00:23:32.920
can imagine.

599
00:23:33.780 --> 00:23:36.020
Her words were like a balm and a

600
00:23:36.020 --> 00:23:37.520
wound at the same time.

601
00:23:37.980 --> 00:23:40.480
She spoke with such sincerity that it was

602
00:23:40.480 --> 00:23:43.580
impossible to feel bitterness, even as her meaning

603
00:23:43.580 --> 00:23:44.280
pierced me.

604
00:23:45.220 --> 00:23:47.680
What you told me about your dreamer, she

605
00:23:47.680 --> 00:23:50.060
continued, is not true anymore.

606
00:23:50.780 --> 00:23:52.420
Not about you, at least.

607
00:23:53.220 --> 00:23:55.240
You've changed, you've recovered.

608
00:23:56.040 --> 00:23:57.900
You're not the same man you described to

609
00:23:57.900 --> 00:23:58.100
me.

610
00:23:59.220 --> 00:24:01.360
She looked at me with something like pride,

611
00:24:01.860 --> 00:24:04.260
as though she were acknowledging a transformation she

612
00:24:04.260 --> 00:24:05.460
herself had brought about.

613
00:24:06.200 --> 00:24:08.220
If you ever fall in love with someone,

614
00:24:08.740 --> 00:24:11.220
really fall in love, I pray that God

615
00:24:11.220 --> 00:24:12.640
grants you happiness with her.

616
00:24:12.640 --> 00:24:15.040
I don't need to wish anything for her,

617
00:24:15.160 --> 00:24:16.800
though, because she will be happy.

618
00:24:17.380 --> 00:24:18.080
I know it.

619
00:24:18.760 --> 00:24:21.560
I'm a woman, after all, and I understand

620
00:24:21.560 --> 00:24:22.200
these things.

621
00:24:22.880 --> 00:24:24.740
Believe me when I tell you this.

622
00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:28.600
She fell silent then, her words hanging in

623
00:24:28.600 --> 00:24:30.960
the air between us, and for a moment

624
00:24:30.960 --> 00:24:32.200
neither of us could speak.

625
00:24:32.920 --> 00:24:35.820
She pressed my hand warmly, her grip firm

626
00:24:35.820 --> 00:24:38.000
yet tender, as though she wanted to convey

627
00:24:38.000 --> 00:24:40.280
everything she couldn't put into words through that

628
00:24:40.280 --> 00:24:41.100
single gesture.

629
00:24:41.740 --> 00:24:44.600
I felt my throat tighten with emotion, but

630
00:24:44.600 --> 00:24:46.180
I couldn't bring myself to respond.

631
00:24:47.040 --> 00:24:50.340
The weight of her words, their bittersweet kindness,

632
00:24:50.940 --> 00:24:51.740
held me silent.

633
00:24:52.920 --> 00:24:56.020
Minutes passed in this quiet shared understanding.

634
00:24:56.980 --> 00:24:59.580
At last she lifted her head and broke

635
00:24:59.580 --> 00:25:00.200
the silence.

636
00:25:01.020 --> 00:25:03.520
It's clear he won't come tonight, she said

637
00:25:03.520 --> 00:25:06.700
softly, her voice steady but tinged with resignation.

638
00:25:07.340 --> 00:25:08.280
It's late now.

639
00:25:09.140 --> 00:25:12.000
I forced myself to reply, summoning all the

640
00:25:12.000 --> 00:25:13.120
conviction I could muster.

641
00:25:13.780 --> 00:25:16.360
He'll come tomorrow, I said firmly, as though

642
00:25:16.360 --> 00:25:18.340
by sheer will I could make it true.

643
00:25:19.360 --> 00:25:22.380
Yes, she said after a pause, and this

644
00:25:22.380 --> 00:25:24.260
time there was no trace of her earlier

645
00:25:24.260 --> 00:25:24.620
doubt.

646
00:25:25.180 --> 00:25:27.240
Her voice was calm, almost cheerful.

647
00:25:28.100 --> 00:25:30.880
I see now that it's impossible for him

648
00:25:30.880 --> 00:25:31.860
to come before tomorrow.

649
00:25:31.860 --> 00:25:35.100
Well, good-bye then, till tomorrow.

650
00:25:35.920 --> 00:25:37.740
If it rains I might not come, but

651
00:25:37.740 --> 00:25:40.280
the day after tomorrow I'll come for certain.

652
00:25:40.980 --> 00:25:43.200
Whatever happens, I'll be here.

653
00:25:43.960 --> 00:25:45.140
Promise me you'll come too.

654
00:25:45.760 --> 00:25:46.940
I need to see you.

655
00:25:47.800 --> 00:25:48.800
I'll tell you everything.

656
00:25:50.040 --> 00:25:52.400
As we parted she gave me her hand

657
00:25:52.400 --> 00:25:55.280
again, this time holding it longer, as though

658
00:25:55.280 --> 00:25:56.680
she was reluctant to let go.

659
00:25:57.360 --> 00:25:59.580
Her eyes met mine with a rare openness,

660
00:26:00.220 --> 00:26:02.480
a kind of pure sincerity that took my

661
00:26:02.480 --> 00:26:03.060
breath away.

662
00:26:03.860 --> 00:26:05.780
We'll always be together, won't we?

663
00:26:06.080 --> 00:26:08.920
she asked candidly, her voice filled with quiet

664
00:26:08.920 --> 00:26:09.280
hope.

665
00:26:10.180 --> 00:26:13.840
Oh, Nastenka, Nastenka, if only you knew how

666
00:26:13.840 --> 00:26:15.220
lonely I am now.

667
00:26:15.980 --> 00:26:18.300
When nine o'clock struck that evening I

668
00:26:18.300 --> 00:26:19.800
couldn't bear to stay indoors.

669
00:26:20.520 --> 00:26:23.460
The hours seemed to stretch endlessly, and the

670
00:26:23.460 --> 00:26:25.320
walls of my room felt like they were

671
00:26:25.320 --> 00:26:26.620
closing in around me.

672
00:26:27.240 --> 00:26:29.460
I put on my coat and stepped outside,

673
00:26:29.880 --> 00:26:31.840
indifferent to the damp chill of the weather.

674
00:26:32.540 --> 00:26:34.680
The rain had eased, but the streets were

675
00:26:34.680 --> 00:26:37.160
still slick and gleaming under the faint glow

676
00:26:37.160 --> 00:26:38.020
of the streetlights.

677
00:26:38.560 --> 00:26:41.460
I walked without direction, my feet carrying me

678
00:26:41.460 --> 00:26:43.400
almost instinctively to the embankment.

679
00:26:44.160 --> 00:26:45.800
There I sat on the bench we had

680
00:26:45.800 --> 00:26:49.100
shared, staring out into the dark, restless waters.

681
00:26:49.940 --> 00:26:52.180
After a while I found myself walking toward

682
00:26:52.180 --> 00:26:52.680
her street.

683
00:26:53.160 --> 00:26:55.660
My heart beat faster with every step, a

684
00:26:55.660 --> 00:26:58.620
strange mix of anticipation and dread building within

685
00:26:58.620 --> 00:26:58.900
me.

686
00:26:59.560 --> 00:27:01.100
But when I was only a few steps

687
00:27:01.100 --> 00:27:03.060
away from her door, I stopped.

688
00:27:03.780 --> 00:27:06.020
Shame washed over me like a cold wave.

689
00:27:06.700 --> 00:27:07.600
What was I doing?

690
00:27:08.480 --> 00:27:10.400
I couldn't bring myself to look at her

691
00:27:10.400 --> 00:27:10.820
windows.

692
00:27:11.400 --> 00:27:14.200
I turned abruptly and walked away, my shoulders

693
00:27:14.200 --> 00:27:16.980
hunched against the damp air, my thoughts heavier

694
00:27:16.980 --> 00:27:17.460
than ever.

695
00:27:18.040 --> 00:27:20.360
I returned home feeling more dejected than I

696
00:27:20.360 --> 00:27:21.320
had ever been before.

697
00:27:21.980 --> 00:27:24.160
The dreary day seemed to reflect my own

698
00:27:24.160 --> 00:27:27.300
desolation, each raindrop a small echo of the

699
00:27:27.300 --> 00:27:28.180
ache in my heart.

700
00:27:28.900 --> 00:27:31.340
If the weather had been fine, perhaps I

701
00:27:31.340 --> 00:27:33.240
would have wandered the streets all night trying

702
00:27:33.240 --> 00:27:35.740
to escape my thoughts, but the rain drove

703
00:27:35.740 --> 00:27:37.680
me back, forcing me to sit with my

704
00:27:37.680 --> 00:27:38.080
loneliness.

705
00:27:38.960 --> 00:27:40.860
Still I clung to the promise of tomorrow.

706
00:27:41.400 --> 00:27:43.900
Tomorrow she would come, and she would tell

707
00:27:43.900 --> 00:27:44.560
me everything.

708
00:27:45.420 --> 00:27:49.540
Tomorrow would bring answers, resolution, perhaps even hope.

709
00:27:50.580 --> 00:27:52.840
The letter hadn't arrived yet, of course, but

710
00:27:52.840 --> 00:27:54.880
I told myself that was to be expected.

711
00:27:55.560 --> 00:27:58.200
By now, I thought bitterly, they must already

712
00:27:58.200 --> 00:27:58.740
be together.
